1
00:00:02,550 --> 00:00:03,551
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,928 --> 00:00:05,929
Earth.

3
00:00:06,846 --> 00:00:07,847
Fire.

4
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:09,891
Air.

5
00:00:11,434 --> 00:00:15,396
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,522 --> 00:00:18,566
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,859 --> 00:00:22,487
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,612 --> 00:00:23,821
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,947 --> 00:00:26,241
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

10
00:00:27,575 --> 00:00:29,702
A hundred years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

11
00:00:29,827 --> 00:00:32,914
the new Avatar,
an Airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:33,039 --> 00:00:35,250
And although
his airbending skills are great,

13
00:00:35,375 --> 00:00:37,669
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:37,794 --> 00:00:39,003
AANG: Oof!

15
00:00:39,128 --> 00:00:42,090
KATARA: But I believe
Aang can save the world.

16
00:00:42,215 --> 00:00:45,718
♪

17
00:00:48,141 --> 00:00:51,228
♪

18
00:01:06,076 --> 00:01:07,535
Top of the morning, Momo!

19
00:01:07,661 --> 00:01:09,037
Sounds like you slept well.

20
00:01:09,162 --> 00:01:10,497
Like a baby moose lion.

21
00:01:10,622 --> 00:01:12,624
I'm ready to face the Fire Lord.

22
00:01:12,749 --> 00:01:14,918
So what's your strategy
for taking him down?

23
00:01:15,043 --> 00:01:16,753
Going to get your glow on
and hit him with

24
00:01:16,878 --> 00:01:18,338
a little Avatar State action?

25
00:01:18,463 --> 00:01:19,547
I can't.

26
00:01:19,673 --> 00:01:21,299
When Azula shot me
with lightning,

27
00:01:21,424 --> 00:01:23,927
my seventh chakra was locked,
cutting off my connection

28
00:01:24,052 --> 00:01:26,263
to all the cosmic energy
in the Universe.

29
00:01:27,138 --> 00:01:28,556
You know what I just heard?

30
00:01:28,682 --> 00:01:32,018
Blah-blah spiritual mumbo jumbo,
blah-blah something about space.

31
00:01:33,270 --> 00:01:34,604
KATARA: Oh no.

32
00:01:34,688 --> 00:01:37,315
Sokka, do you think the fog
will delay the invasion?

33
00:01:38,566 --> 00:01:41,403
No, that is the invasion.

34
00:01:41,528 --> 00:01:46,992
♪

35
00:01:52,122 --> 00:01:53,707
KATARA: You made it, Dad!

36
00:01:53,832 --> 00:01:56,084
Were you able to locate
everyone I told you to find?

37
00:01:56,376 --> 00:01:59,129
I did, but I'm
a little worried, Sokka.

38
00:01:59,254 --> 00:02:01,881
Some of these men
aren't exactly the warrior type.

39
00:02:02,007 --> 00:02:04,092
Whooo-wheee.

40
00:02:04,217 --> 00:02:06,636
This place ain't nothing
like a swamp.

41
00:02:06,761 --> 00:02:08,263
What'd you reckon that is, Tho?

42
00:02:08,388 --> 00:02:09,889
Some sort of Fire Nation
exploding trap

43
00:02:10,015 --> 00:02:11,224
that would eat ya?

44
00:02:11,349 --> 00:02:13,143
It's just a rock, Due.

45
00:02:13,268 --> 00:02:15,520
Well, I'll be.

46
00:02:15,645 --> 00:02:17,439
Is it just me,
or are those fellas

47
00:02:17,564 --> 00:02:19,357
a little loose in the leaf hat?

48
00:02:19,482 --> 00:02:22,110
I just wish
they would wear pants.

49
00:02:22,235 --> 00:02:24,404
Pants are an illusion.

50
00:02:24,529 --> 00:02:26,364
And so is death.

51
00:02:28,658 --> 00:02:29,993
HARU: Hi, Katara.

52
00:02:32,037 --> 00:02:34,247
Haru, it's so good to see you.

53
00:02:34,372 --> 00:02:35,790
Toph, this is Haru.

54
00:02:35,915 --> 00:02:38,168
When we met him, his town was
controlled by the Fire Nation.

55
00:02:38,293 --> 00:02:39,878
So we had to hide
his Earth-bending.

56
00:02:40,003 --> 00:02:43,340
Katara inspired me and my
father to take back our village.

57
00:02:43,465 --> 00:02:46,259
You helped us find
our courage, Katara.

58
00:02:46,384 --> 00:02:48,928
Now we're here to help you.

59
00:02:50,305 --> 00:02:52,849
No way. Is that―

60
00:02:53,058 --> 00:02:55,935
Hippo happy
to see Blind Bandit!

61
00:02:56,061 --> 00:02:57,729
You guys here for a rematch?

62
00:02:57,854 --> 00:02:59,397
Negatory.

63
00:02:59,522 --> 00:03:02,650
The Boulder and The Hippo
no longer fight

64
00:03:02,776 --> 00:03:04,486
for others' entertainment.

65
00:03:04,611 --> 00:03:07,530
Now, we fight for our Kingdom!

66
00:03:08,031 --> 00:03:09,366
Sweet!

67
00:03:09,491 --> 00:03:11,326
♪

68
00:03:11,618 --> 00:03:13,370
[ crash ]

69
00:03:15,205 --> 00:03:18,875
[ coughing ]

70
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:24,464
Was that a new invention?

71
00:03:24,589 --> 00:03:25,924
Yes.

72
00:03:26,049 --> 00:03:29,552
But unfortunately,
the incendiary capabilities

73
00:03:29,677 --> 00:03:32,514
of peanut sauce
proved to be a failure.

74
00:03:32,639 --> 00:03:34,599
You're making
peanut sauce bombs?

75
00:03:34,724 --> 00:03:35,892
They're destructive.

76
00:03:36,017 --> 00:03:37,560
And delicious!

77
00:03:37,685 --> 00:03:39,938
BOTH: [ slurps and laughs ]

78
00:03:40,146 --> 00:03:42,399
Were you able to complete work
on the plans I sent you?

79
00:03:42,732 --> 00:03:44,025
Yes, I was.

80
00:03:44,150 --> 00:03:47,278
And I think the Fire Nation
will be quite surprised.

81
00:03:47,404 --> 00:03:49,614
Aang, my dad and I
made this for you.

82
00:03:49,739 --> 00:03:53,576
♪

83
00:03:53,701 --> 00:03:54,744
A new glider!

84
00:03:54,869 --> 00:03:56,371
This is amazing.

85
00:03:56,496 --> 00:04:00,291
And as a special feature,
I added a snack compartment.

86
00:04:02,419 --> 00:04:04,879
Oh well, I'm sure
that will come in handy.

87
00:04:07,841 --> 00:04:10,844
I bet you're tired of
being in that cell, old man.

88
00:04:10,969 --> 00:04:12,804
Well, too bad.

89
00:04:12,929 --> 00:04:16,099
You're never stepping
outside these walls again.

90
00:04:16,224 --> 00:04:17,684
Breakfast.

91
00:04:18,935 --> 00:04:20,270
Don't get too close.

92
00:04:20,395 --> 00:04:22,480
His stench will
knock you right out.

93
00:04:22,605 --> 00:04:23,940
[ chuckles ]

94
00:04:25,442 --> 00:04:27,235
I snuck in some white jade tea.

95
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:30,113
I know you like rare teas.

96
00:04:30,238 --> 00:04:31,865
IROH: Thank you, Ming.

97
00:04:31,990 --> 00:04:36,619
Ever since I was put in here,
you have been very kind to me.

98
00:04:36,744 --> 00:04:41,416
♪

99
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,126
[ gulps nervously ]

100
00:04:43,251 --> 00:04:45,295
Don't worry, you'll do great.

101
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:48,506
[ deep breath ]

102
00:04:48,631 --> 00:04:49,632
Good morning, everyone!

103
00:04:49,757 --> 00:04:50,884
Ah!

104
00:04:53,595 --> 00:04:55,013
Um...

105
00:04:55,138 --> 00:04:58,975
So, as you know, today
we're invading the Fire Nation.

106
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:00,393
I mean I know you know that.

107
00:05:00,518 --> 00:05:01,895
Because otherwise why else
would you be here.

108
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:03,688
[ laughs ] Anyway...

109
00:05:06,858 --> 00:05:08,359
The Fire Lord's palace is here.

110
00:05:08,485 --> 00:05:10,987
Uh no, uh wait―uh
wait―uh wait, it's here.

111
00:05:11,112 --> 00:05:12,864
And, uh, there's
an eclipse today.

112
00:05:12,989 --> 00:05:14,657
And Aang's going
to fight the Fire Lord.

113
00:05:14,782 --> 00:05:16,868
And the Firebenders
won't have any fire to use,

114
00:05:16,951 --> 00:05:18,244
so that's good for us.

115
00:05:18,328 --> 00:05:22,540
And um―I'm sorry, let me
start at the beginning.

116
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:25,502
Katara and I discovered
Aang frozen in an iceberg.

117
00:05:25,627 --> 00:05:27,962
Now I didn't like Aang at first,
but I grew to love him over time,

118
00:05:28,087 --> 00:05:29,255
then we went over
to the Southern Air Temple,

119
00:05:29,339 --> 00:05:30,798
where Aang used to live,
and then we met Suki,

120
00:05:30,882 --> 00:05:33,426
-who is a Kyoshi warrior.
- Wow, when he says beginning,

121
00:05:33,510 --> 00:05:35,428
he means
the beginning beginning.

122
00:05:35,553 --> 00:05:37,722
SOKKA: ...got Haru arrested, and
then now he's grown a mustache.

123
00:05:37,847 --> 00:05:40,391
- And if you look in the front―
- HAKODA: Thank you, Sokka.

124
00:05:40,517 --> 00:05:43,394
It's okay, why don't
you take a break?

125
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:46,189
Let me just clarify
a few points for everyone.

126
00:05:46,314 --> 00:05:49,150
Today is the Day of Black Sun.

127
00:05:49,275 --> 00:05:51,694
And I want to thank you all
for your self-sacrifice

128
00:05:51,819 --> 00:05:53,404
and your courage.

129
00:05:53,530 --> 00:05:55,365
There are two steps
to the invasion.

130
00:05:55,490 --> 00:05:58,701
A naval stage
and then a land stage.

131
00:05:58,826 --> 00:06:01,120
To gain sea access
to the Fire Nation capital,

132
00:06:01,246 --> 00:06:05,083
we have to get past
our first major obstacle here.

133
00:06:05,208 --> 00:06:07,210
The Great Gates of Azulon.

134
00:06:07,335 --> 00:06:10,046
Next, we hit the land,
and we hit hard.

135
00:06:10,171 --> 00:06:11,631
We must fight
past their battlements

136
00:06:11,756 --> 00:06:13,925
and secure the plaza tower.

137
00:06:14,050 --> 00:06:16,719
Once we do that,
it's up to the royal palace.

138
00:06:16,844 --> 00:06:19,013
At that point,
the eclipse will begin.

139
00:06:19,556 --> 00:06:20,974
Excuse me.

140
00:06:21,099 --> 00:06:23,476
The Boulder is confused.

141
00:06:23,601 --> 00:06:27,063
Isn't the point to invade
during the eclipse?

142
00:06:27,188 --> 00:06:29,899
When the Firebenders
are powerless?

143
00:06:30,024 --> 00:06:32,026
The eclipse
only lasts eight minutes.

144
00:06:32,151 --> 00:06:34,028
Not enough time
for the whole invasion.

145
00:06:34,153 --> 00:06:37,198
And the royal palace is heavily
guarded by Firebenders.

146
00:06:37,323 --> 00:06:40,243
So that's where we'll need
the eclipse advantage the most.

147
00:06:40,368 --> 00:06:42,662
When this is finished,
the Avatar

148
00:06:42,787 --> 00:06:44,872
would have defeated
the Fire Lord.

149
00:06:45,206 --> 00:06:47,917
We would have control
of the Fire Nation capital.

150
00:06:48,042 --> 00:06:50,920
And this war will be over!

151
00:06:51,045 --> 00:06:56,759
[ crowd cheering ]

152
00:06:56,884 --> 00:06:59,512
♪

153
00:07:11,816 --> 00:07:13,443
[ roars ]

154
00:07:13,568 --> 00:07:17,405
♪

155
00:07:24,996 --> 00:07:26,247
[ sheep baas ]

156
00:07:26,372 --> 00:07:32,170
♪

157
00:07:41,554 --> 00:07:45,725
♪

158
00:07:54,150 --> 00:07:55,568
We've been looking
everywhere for you.

159
00:07:55,693 --> 00:07:57,362
The boats are ready to leave.

160
00:07:57,487 --> 00:07:58,988
I messed up, Aang.

161
00:07:59,113 --> 00:08:00,323
What?

162
00:08:00,448 --> 00:08:02,617
The invasion plan
was my moment of truth.

163
00:08:02,742 --> 00:08:04,869
And I completely flopped it.

164
00:08:04,994 --> 00:08:07,705
I just...fell apart.

165
00:08:07,789 --> 00:08:10,458
Sokka, that speech wasn't
your moment of truth.

166
00:08:10,625 --> 00:08:11,959
That was just public speaking,

167
00:08:12,085 --> 00:08:13,836
and nobody's really good
at that.

168
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:15,338
My dad is.

169
00:08:15,505 --> 00:08:18,299
He explained the plan perfectly
and inspired everyone.

170
00:08:18,424 --> 00:08:20,259
Like a real leader should.

171
00:08:20,385 --> 00:08:21,803
Look, your moment of truth

172
00:08:21,928 --> 00:08:24,055
isn't going to be
in front of some map.

173
00:08:24,180 --> 00:08:26,391
It's going to be out there
on the battlefield.

174
00:08:26,683 --> 00:08:28,643
You seem so confident
about everything.

175
00:08:28,768 --> 00:08:30,436
How do you know
we're going to win?

176
00:08:30,561 --> 00:08:33,314
Because I already failed
the world once at Ba Sing Se.

177
00:08:33,439 --> 00:08:35,316
I won't let myself fail again.

178
00:08:35,441 --> 00:08:39,112
♪

179
00:08:41,781 --> 00:08:42,824
BATO: There they are.

180
00:08:42,949 --> 00:08:44,867
The Great Gates of Azulon.

181
00:08:44,992 --> 00:08:47,120
KATARA: I don't
see any gates.

182
00:08:47,245 --> 00:08:48,788
Katara,
you and the Swamp-Benders

183
00:08:48,913 --> 00:08:50,456
whip up a fog cover.

184
00:08:50,581 --> 00:08:52,834
We'll sneak by that statues
just like we sneaked by

185
00:08:52,959 --> 00:08:54,669
that fire navy blockade.

186
00:08:54,794 --> 00:08:57,380
♪

187
00:09:05,471 --> 00:09:07,765
Keep it up,
we're almost through.

188
00:09:07,890 --> 00:09:12,353
[ alarm ringing ]

189
00:09:14,105 --> 00:09:16,357
[ fire blazing ]

190
00:09:16,858 --> 00:09:21,738
♪

191
00:09:34,083 --> 00:09:35,835
[ fire blazing ]

192
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:38,755
♪

193
00:09:38,838 --> 00:09:40,381
[ motors revving ]

194
00:09:40,590 --> 00:09:41,924
Everyone below deck.

195
00:09:44,343 --> 00:09:46,262
Let's hope your invention works.

196
00:09:46,387 --> 00:09:51,476
♪

197
00:10:06,407 --> 00:10:08,367
[ crash ]

198
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:12,663
No one's on board, Sir.

199
00:10:12,747 --> 00:10:13,790
Where'd they go?

200
00:10:13,998 --> 00:10:19,921
♪

201
00:10:26,052 --> 00:10:28,095
You really outdone
yourself this time, son.

202
00:10:28,221 --> 00:10:29,222
TOPH: Yeah.

203
00:10:29,347 --> 00:10:31,307
Congratulations, Sokka.

204
00:10:31,432 --> 00:10:34,852
You managed to invent a worse
way of travel than flying.

205
00:10:34,977 --> 00:10:36,187
Helmet?

206
00:10:36,312 --> 00:10:37,396
[ vomits ]

207
00:10:37,522 --> 00:10:38,815
Well, I just came up
with the idea.

208
00:10:38,898 --> 00:10:40,233
The Mechanist did all the work.

209
00:10:40,358 --> 00:10:42,443
But don't sell
yourself short, my boy.

210
00:10:42,568 --> 00:10:45,530
It was your idea
to use water-bending

211
00:10:45,655 --> 00:10:48,115
to make the subs sink and float.

212
00:10:48,241 --> 00:10:49,325
Brilliant!

213
00:10:49,450 --> 00:10:51,327
Though your original designs

214
00:10:51,452 --> 00:10:54,288
were a bit difficult
to decipher.

215
00:10:54,705 --> 00:10:57,750
Unfortunately, there is
one problem I couldn't fix.

216
00:10:58,125 --> 00:11:00,753
The subs have
a limited air supply.

217
00:11:00,878 --> 00:11:04,590
Before we land on the beaches,
we'll need to resurface.

218
00:11:06,926 --> 00:11:09,971
Lunchtime, General Iroh.

219
00:11:10,096 --> 00:11:12,807
And this time, I brought you
an extra bowl of rice.

220
00:11:12,932 --> 00:11:14,767
Thank you, Ming.

221
00:11:14,892 --> 00:11:17,603
Your little gestures of kindness

222
00:11:17,728 --> 00:11:21,315
have made my days in prison
bearable.

223
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:24,944
I think you should take
the rest of the day off.

224
00:11:25,069 --> 00:11:28,114
- What?
- You don't look well.

225
00:11:28,239 --> 00:11:31,242
Maybe you should
go home and rest.

226
00:11:31,367 --> 00:11:33,202
No, I feel fine.

227
00:11:33,327 --> 00:11:34,579
Trust me.

228
00:11:34,704 --> 00:11:38,666
It is better that you are
not here this afternoon.

229
00:11:38,791 --> 00:11:44,422
♪

230
00:11:54,724 --> 00:11:56,851
So, this is it, huh?

231
00:11:57,226 --> 00:11:58,853
Are you ready
for the Fire Nation to know

232
00:11:58,936 --> 00:12:00,479
the Avatar's alive?

233
00:12:00,563 --> 00:12:01,689
I'm ready.

234
00:12:01,772 --> 00:12:06,027
♪

235
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:09,572
I hope you kick some serious
Fire Lord butt, twinkle toes.

236
00:12:09,739 --> 00:12:11,240
HAKODA: Everyone, listen up.

237
00:12:11,699 --> 00:12:14,660
The next time we resurface,
it'll be on the beaches.

238
00:12:14,785 --> 00:12:16,829
So stay alert and fight smart.

239
00:12:17,121 --> 00:12:19,248
Now break time's over,
back in the subs.

240
00:12:19,415 --> 00:12:23,377
♪

241
00:12:26,130 --> 00:12:28,132
- Aang, I―
- Katara, I―

242
00:12:28,257 --> 00:12:29,675
You go first.

243
00:12:30,635 --> 00:12:33,054
We've been through
so many things together.

244
00:12:33,179 --> 00:12:35,806
And I've seen you
grow up so much.

245
00:12:36,098 --> 00:12:39,393
You're not that little goofy kid
I found in the iceberg anymore.

246
00:12:39,602 --> 00:12:41,312
I guess
what I'm trying to say is

247
00:12:41,437 --> 00:12:43,356
I'm really proud of you.

248
00:12:45,232 --> 00:12:47,401
Everything is going to be
different after today, isn't it?

249
00:12:47,526 --> 00:12:48,903
Yes, it is.

250
00:12:49,904 --> 00:12:52,990
What if―what if
I don't come back?

251
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,742
Aang, don't say that.

252
00:12:54,867 --> 00:12:56,243
Of course you'll―

253
00:12:56,369 --> 00:13:01,666
♪

254
00:13:08,673 --> 00:13:09,674
Katara, what are you doing?

255
00:13:09,799 --> 00:13:11,217
It's time to submerge.

256
00:13:11,342 --> 00:13:13,594
What? Right, I'm on it.

257
00:13:13,719 --> 00:13:18,432
♪

258
00:13:18,557 --> 00:13:20,810
[ growls ]

259
00:13:20,935 --> 00:13:26,315
♪

260
00:13:29,777 --> 00:13:33,114
♪

261
00:13:33,239 --> 00:13:35,074
I'm sorry, Mai.

262
00:13:35,199 --> 00:13:41,122
♪

263
00:13:50,256 --> 00:13:51,340
[ munching ]

264
00:13:51,424 --> 00:13:52,466
What do you know?

265
00:13:52,550 --> 00:13:53,843
It did come in handy.

266
00:13:53,968 --> 00:13:59,932
♪

267
00:14:04,854 --> 00:14:05,980
Everyone in position.

268
00:14:06,105 --> 00:14:07,857
Earthbenders, into your tanks.

269
00:14:07,982 --> 00:14:09,608
This is going to be
a rough ride.

270
00:14:09,734 --> 00:14:14,947
♪

271
00:14:19,994 --> 00:14:23,039
[ alarm sounding ]

272
00:14:23,164 --> 00:14:27,501
♪

273
00:14:32,506 --> 00:14:36,594
[ crash and water rushing ]

274
00:14:36,802 --> 00:14:41,182
♪

275
00:14:48,272 --> 00:14:50,191
[ splash ]

276
00:14:50,775 --> 00:14:56,739
♪

277
00:14:57,323 --> 00:14:58,783
Ready the torpedo.

278
00:14:59,116 --> 00:15:02,536
♪

279
00:15:02,661 --> 00:15:04,288
Launch!

280
00:15:04,371 --> 00:15:07,249
♪

281
00:15:07,541 --> 00:15:11,629
[ explosion ]

282
00:15:12,296 --> 00:15:18,010
♪

283
00:15:28,771 --> 00:15:30,397
[ sighs ]

284
00:15:32,525 --> 00:15:37,321
[ missiles blasting ]

285
00:15:37,822 --> 00:15:44,120
♪

286
00:15:49,667 --> 00:15:50,751
MEN: [ screaming ]

287
00:15:55,464 --> 00:15:58,592
[ gunfire erupting ]

288
00:15:58,717 --> 00:16:04,223
♪

289
00:16:04,348 --> 00:16:08,936
[ gunfire continues ]

290
00:16:09,311 --> 00:16:14,567
♪

291
00:16:21,532 --> 00:16:22,992
[ roars ]

292
00:16:23,075 --> 00:16:28,664
♪

293
00:16:28,747 --> 00:16:29,874
[ fire blasts ]

294
00:16:29,999 --> 00:16:31,667
♪

295
00:16:31,792 --> 00:16:33,586
[ fire blasts ]

296
00:16:33,711 --> 00:16:40,509
♪

297
00:16:40,634 --> 00:16:43,262
[ metal crashing ]

298
00:16:43,387 --> 00:16:48,517
♪

299
00:16:57,526 --> 00:16:59,778
[ blast ]

300
00:16:59,904 --> 00:17:01,405
We're a man down.

301
00:17:01,530 --> 00:17:03,199
Where in tarnation is Hue?

302
00:17:05,242 --> 00:17:07,453
[ splash ]

303
00:17:07,578 --> 00:17:13,500
♪

304
00:17:21,717 --> 00:17:24,136
Hey Hue, where you been?

305
00:17:25,763 --> 00:17:27,890
Communing with nature.

306
00:17:28,015 --> 00:17:30,935
Takes a while to collect
this much seaweed.

307
00:17:31,060 --> 00:17:35,940
♪

308
00:17:46,075 --> 00:17:47,785
[ grunts ]

309
00:17:47,910 --> 00:17:49,370
Dad, look out!

310
00:17:49,495 --> 00:17:55,334
[ grunting ]

311
00:17:55,459 --> 00:18:00,756
♪

312
00:18:05,261 --> 00:18:07,179
[ explosion ]

313
00:18:07,304 --> 00:18:13,227
♪

314
00:18:13,352 --> 00:18:15,396
[ explosion ]

315
00:18:15,521 --> 00:18:17,523
Sokka, we've got
to take out those battlements.

316
00:18:17,648 --> 00:18:19,024
It's our only chance.

317
00:18:19,149 --> 00:18:20,484
I've got an idea.

318
00:18:20,609 --> 00:18:24,822
♪

319
00:18:24,947 --> 00:18:26,824
[ metal dings ]

320
00:18:26,949 --> 00:18:29,326
[ fuses sizzle ]

321
00:18:29,451 --> 00:18:30,828
♪

322
00:18:30,953 --> 00:18:32,037
MEN: Ah!

323
00:18:32,162 --> 00:18:37,626
♪

324
00:18:37,751 --> 00:18:39,378
Ah, ah!

325
00:18:39,503 --> 00:18:42,089
♪

326
00:18:42,214 --> 00:18:44,091
[ roaring ]

327
00:18:44,216 --> 00:18:45,467
You two take out
that battlement.

328
00:18:45,592 --> 00:18:46,635
I've got this one.

329
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:48,137
Watch each other's backs.

330
00:18:48,262 --> 00:18:50,347
♪

331
00:18:50,472 --> 00:18:52,099
[ metal clings ]

332
00:18:52,224 --> 00:18:54,226
[ water rushing ]

333
00:18:54,351 --> 00:18:58,897
♪

334
00:18:59,023 --> 00:19:00,983
[ explosion ]

335
00:19:01,108 --> 00:19:05,279
♪

336
00:19:05,404 --> 00:19:08,407
[ grunting ]

337
00:19:08,532 --> 00:19:11,035
♪

338
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:14,455
[ grunting ]

339
00:19:15,914 --> 00:19:17,082
Dad?

340
00:19:17,207 --> 00:19:18,250
Dad!

341
00:19:18,375 --> 00:19:22,504
♪

342
00:19:24,923 --> 00:19:27,760
I know I've made
some bad choices.

343
00:19:27,885 --> 00:19:29,428
But today...

344
00:19:29,553 --> 00:19:31,013
I'm gonna set things right.

345
00:19:31,138 --> 00:19:35,809
♪

346
00:19:41,982 --> 00:19:43,692
[ roars ]

347
00:19:43,817 --> 00:19:47,237
♪

348
00:19:47,363 --> 00:19:49,073
[ grunts ]

349
00:19:49,198 --> 00:19:52,993
[ water rushing ]

350
00:19:53,118 --> 00:19:54,495
KATARA: How does that feel, Dad?

351
00:19:54,620 --> 00:19:56,955
HAKODA: A-a little better.

352
00:19:57,081 --> 00:19:59,541
I need to get
back...to the troops.

353
00:19:59,666 --> 00:20:00,667
[ moaning ]

354
00:20:00,793 --> 00:20:02,544
KATARA: You're hurt...badly.

355
00:20:02,669 --> 00:20:04,088
You can't fight anymore.

356
00:20:04,588 --> 00:20:07,674
Everyone's counting on me
to lead this mission, Katara.

357
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:10,094
I won't let them down.

358
00:20:10,219 --> 00:20:11,428
[ grunts ]

359
00:20:11,970 --> 00:20:13,847
Can't you heal him any faster?

360
00:20:13,972 --> 00:20:15,641
I'm doing everything I can.

361
00:20:15,766 --> 00:20:19,520
♪

362
00:20:19,645 --> 00:20:20,687
I'll do it.

363
00:20:21,063 --> 00:20:24,483
No offense, Sokka, but you're
not exactly Mr. Healing Hands.

364
00:20:24,775 --> 00:20:27,403
No, I'll lead
the invasion force.

365
00:20:27,611 --> 00:20:29,279
Don't be crazy, Sokka.

366
00:20:29,446 --> 00:20:32,449
Maybe I am a little crazy but
the eclipse is about to start,

367
00:20:32,574 --> 00:20:35,160
and we need to be up that
volcano by the time it does.

368
00:20:35,285 --> 00:20:37,037
HAKODA: You can do this.

369
00:20:37,621 --> 00:20:39,873
I'm proud of you, son.

370
00:20:41,166 --> 00:20:43,210
I still think you're crazy.

371
00:20:43,335 --> 00:20:44,837
But I'm proud of you, too.

372
00:20:44,962 --> 00:20:50,467
♪

373
00:20:50,592 --> 00:20:51,718
Yip yip.

374
00:20:51,844 --> 00:20:54,096
[ growls ]

375
00:20:54,221 --> 00:20:58,183
♪

376
00:20:58,308 --> 00:21:03,856
[ gunfire exploding ]

377
00:21:03,981 --> 00:21:06,942
♪

378
00:21:07,067 --> 00:21:08,652
Listen up, everyone!

379
00:21:08,777 --> 00:21:11,113
I want the tanks
in wedge formation!

380
00:21:11,238 --> 00:21:13,615
Warriors and benders
in the middle.

381
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:16,452
We're taking that tower and
headed for the royal palace!

382
00:21:16,577 --> 00:21:21,957
♪

383
00:21:22,082 --> 00:21:24,501
[ gunfire exploding ]

384
00:21:24,626 --> 00:21:26,295
Charge!

385
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:29,798
♪

386
00:21:31,675 --> 00:21:36,138
♪

387
00:21:43,729 --> 00:21:44,980
That's strange.

388
00:21:45,105 --> 00:21:49,776
♪

389
00:21:52,070 --> 00:21:53,280
[ door opens ]

390
00:21:53,405 --> 00:21:55,324
The Avatar is back!

391
00:22:00,329 --> 00:22:02,247
Hello?

392
00:22:02,372 --> 00:22:03,624
Anyone home?

393
00:22:04,082 --> 00:22:08,587
[ gunfire exploding ]

394
00:22:08,712 --> 00:22:13,342
♪

395
00:22:20,766 --> 00:22:24,269
[ explosion ]

396
00:22:24,394 --> 00:22:27,272
♪

397
00:22:27,397 --> 00:22:29,775
MEN: [ screaming ]

398
00:22:29,900 --> 00:22:34,154
[ gunfire exploding ]

399
00:22:34,279 --> 00:22:36,782
The Fire Nation
is falling back!

400
00:22:36,907 --> 00:22:38,867
♪

401
00:22:38,992 --> 00:22:41,870
Sokka, we're on
our way to victory.

402
00:22:41,995 --> 00:22:46,333
♪

403
00:22:57,636 --> 00:22:58,971
No.

404
00:22:59,096 --> 00:23:00,639
♪

405
00:23:00,764 --> 00:23:04,726
No, no, no!

406
00:23:04,851 --> 00:23:08,313
Fire Lord Ozai, where are you?

407
00:23:08,438 --> 00:23:09,898
♪

408
00:23:17,378 --> 00:23:21,883
MALE:
[ vocalizing drumbeats ]

409
00:23:27,805 --> 00:23:34,521
♪

410
00:23:50,870 --> 00:23:57,377
♪
